(4264630, 614722, 58691, '<td valign="top">This is cute and I like the perspective. More light hitting the left side of her face would help this shot a bit.</td>', 'This is cute and I like the perspective. More light hitting the left side of her face would help this shot a bit.', '2007-11-22 12:55:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264632, 614713, 58691, '<td valign="top">Nice shot. I like the use of greyscale here.</td>', 'Nice shot. I like the use of greyscale here.', '2007-11-22 12:56:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264633, 614644, 58691, '<td valign="top">I like the dramatic effect that the long column of liquid adds to this shot. Focus and contrast are good, but the pink at the bottom of the image is a distraction.</td>', 'I like the dramatic effect that the long column of liquid adds to this shot. Focus and contrast are good, but the pink at the bottom of the image is a distraction.', '2007-11-22 12:57:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264635, 614126, 58691, '<td valign="top">Would like to see the focus on the front runner instead of the pack. Otherwise, this is a decent capture.</td>', 'Would like to see the focus on the front runner instead of the pack. Otherwise, this is a decent capture.', '2007-11-22 12:58:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264646, 613117, 58691, '<td valign="top">Well executed. This is one of the better water balloon shots.</td>', 'Well executed. This is one of the better water balloon shots.', '2007-11-22 13:17:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264651, 613598, 81382, '<td valign="top">Really good capture of the water, not that easily repeatable, some entries in this challenge I imagine people were fiddling with dripping taps all day but you may have only had a few seconds to get this shot done so well done. Not sure about the border, perhaps picking out an average colour of the water spray (yellowey white) would have made the border more part of the image. Good composition though</td>', 'Really good capture of the water, not that easily repeatable, some entries in this challenge I imagine people were fiddling with dripping taps all day but you may have only had a few seconds to get this shot done so well done. Not sure about the border, perhaps picking out an average colour of the water spray (yellowey white) would have made the border more part of the image. Good composition though', '2007-11-22 13:21:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264657, 614572, 81382, '<td valign="top">Composition wise, you might want to consider haveing the dart more to the left and the empty space on the right hand side for the dart to "fly into". Nice and sharp though and neutral background keeps it nice and simple. Interesting border</td>', 'Composition wise, you might want to consider haveing the dart more to the left and the empty space on the right hand side for the dart to "fly into". Nice and sharp though and neutral background keeps it nice and simple. Interesting border', '2007-11-22 13:23:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264662, 614575, 81382, '<td valign="top">Great colours and angle. Could have been made even more interesting by not havingt taken the shot for eye level, a much lower angle would have been wicked.</td>', 'Great colours and angle. Could have been made even more interesting by not havingt taken the shot for eye level, a much lower angle would have been wicked.', '2007-11-22 13:24:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264667, 614450, 81382, '<td valign="top">Just seems a little overly setup and doesn''t convey stopped motion. The "supposedly" moving thing should be the main focus and it only takes up a very small percentage of the image area.</td>', 'Just seems a little overly setup and doesn''t convey stopped motion. The "supposedly" moving thing should be the main focus and it only takes up a very small percentage of the image area.', '2007-11-22 13:26:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264674, 614546, 81382, '<td valign="top">A bit more sharpening after you had sized for the submissing would have really brought out the highlights on the crest of the wave. After resizing I always apply USM with 100, 0.5, 0 settings.</td>', 'A bit more sharpening after you had sized for the submissing would have really brought out the highlights on the crest of the wave. After resizing I always apply USM with 100, 0.5, 0 settings.', '2007-11-22 13:28:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264679, 613783, 81382, '<td valign="top">Nice DOF and lovely rich colours. Could have cropped onto the main falling leaf a bit more and although the leaves on the left are nice, they are not nessessarily in motion to the same extent and are taking the eye off the stopped motion which afterall is the whole point. You almost have two subjects, the leaf on the right and the rest of the stuff on the left which makes for a divided image and doesn''t permit great composition.</td>', 'Nice DOF and lovely rich colours. Could have cropped onto the main falling leaf a bit more and although the leaves on the left are nice, they are not nessessarily in motion to the same extent and are taking the eye off the stopped motion which afterall is the whole point. You almost have two subjects, the leaf on the right and the rest of the stuff on the left which makes for a divided image and doesn''t permit great composition.', '2007-11-22 13:32:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264680, 613117, 81382, '<td valign="top">Trying to figure out what has burst. Lovely and sharp and uncomplicated.</td>', 'Trying to figure out what has burst. Lovely and sharp and uncomplicated.', '2007-11-22 13:33:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264682, 614714, 81382, '<td valign="top">Two main subjects at opposite sides of the image. The eyes attention is divided between the two and so IMO the composition is not great. Distracting background and the ball on string is a further complication. I think just a stunning portrait of just one of the girls jumping with the feet clealy off the ground with hair flying about, no ball, neutral background and well composed would score so much higher</td>', 'Two main subjects at opposite sides of the image. The eyes attention is divided between the two and so IMO the composition is not great. Distracting background and the ball on string is a further complication. I think just a stunning portrait of just one of the girls jumping with the feet clealy off the ground with hair flying about, no ball, neutral background and well composed would score so much higher', '2007-11-22 13:37:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264683, 614691, 81382, '<td valign="top">Surrounding leaves are sharper than the dog. The tree on the left is a distration.</td>', 'Surrounding leaves are sharper than the dog. The tree on the left is a distration.', '2007-11-22 13:37:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264684, 614700, 81382, '<td valign="top">Could have done with a few more of the leaves being sharper. If none were properly in focus then this entry would be a disaster and you only have maybe 2 or 3 (at least the freefall ones) spot on.</td>', 'Could have done with a few more of the leaves being sharper. If none were properly in focus then this entry would be a disaster and you only have maybe 2 or 3 (at least the freefall ones) spot on.', '2007-11-22 13:39:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264687, 613657, 81382, '<td valign="top">Interesting angle and lighting. I love the colours of the socks against the darkness. If only there was no ground or plant life on the right and just sky instead and this is a distraction.</td>', 'Interesting angle and lighting. I love the colours of the socks against the darkness. If only there was no ground or plant life on the right and just sky instead and this is a distraction.', '2007-11-22 13:41:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264690, 614632, 81382, '<td valign="top">Composition wise, the head is in the centre and even the percieved centre of mass is towards the centre. Having more open space on the right hand side would place the bird a third in from the left (rule of thirds) and have a nice open space to "fly into" which is a double winner for composition. Nice sharp capture though and uncomplicated background so nice and simple with no distractions</td>', 'Composition wise, the head is in the centre and even the percieved centre of mass is towards the centre. Having more open space on the right hand side would place the bird a third in from the left (rule of thirds) and have a nice open space to "fly into" which is a double winner for composition. Nice sharp capture though and uncomplicated background so nice and simple with no distractions', '2007-11-22 13:43:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264693, 614671, 81382, '<td valign="top">What were you thinking with that background, its far too distracting, a nice simple, neutral background would have been far superior. The colours in the background are dull and really let the main subject down. Perhaps if you had greater DOF to make the dice sharper and the background more blurred, then converted to mono / duotone and push the contrast hard then IMO this might have been saved.</td>', 'What were you thinking with that background, its far too distracting, a nice simple, neutral background would have been far superior. The colours in the background are dull and really let the main subject down. Perhaps if you had greater DOF to make the dice sharper and the background more blurred, then converted to mono / duotone and push the contrast hard then IMO this might have been saved.', '2007-11-22 13:46:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264694, 614144, 81382, '<td valign="top">Great colours. The feeling of suspended motion is rather lost though, the plane takes up a very small percentage area of the image.</td>', 'Great colours. The feeling of suspended motion is rather lost though, the plane takes up a very small percentage area of the image.', '2007-11-22 13:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264697, 613913, 81382, '<td valign="top">Great sharpness, uncomplicated background and unless this bird was in an avary or hovering around all day you might only have had a very short period to get this right, unlike the people that can setup a dripping tap and shoot splashes for hours. Great colours, well exposed, a bit more open space on the left to put the bird a third in from the right, plus, the bird appears be moving from right into space on the left and so this might have improved composition two-fold. The best entry I''ve seen so far</td>', 'Great sharpness, uncomplicated background and unless this bird was in an avary or hovering around all day you might only have had a very short period to get this right, unlike the people that can setup a dripping tap and shoot splashes for hours. Great colours, well exposed, a bit more open space on the left to put the bird a third in from the right, plus, the bird appears be moving from right into space on the left and so this might have improved composition two-fold. The best entry I''ve seen so far', '2007-11-22 13:50:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264698, 614630, 81382, '<td valign="top">Cropping in on the drop might not be a bad idea. It is quite small and a little lost against the vast black background. To be able to see the reflection of the leaf in the drop would have been great</td>', 'Cropping in on the drop might not be a bad idea. It is quite small and a little lost against the vast black background. To be able to see the reflection of the leaf in the drop would have been great', '2007-11-22 13:51:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264700, 614383, 81382, '<td valign="top">Spoilt only by the background. If this had been taken from ground level you might have been able to get the sky as the background which would have made for a much cleaner, neutral composition, putting the focus plainly on the bird and also you would have had an amazing angle</td>', 'Spoilt only by the background. If this had been taken from ground level you might have been able to get the sky as the background which would have made for a much cleaner, neutral composition, putting the focus plainly on the bird and also you would have had an amazing angle', '2007-11-22 13:54:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264705, 614556, 81382, '<td valign="top">A lovely wide angle is a little cliche for planes but works so well. Lovely sky colours and foreground detail. Perhaps a lower camera positon to the ground would have increased the foreground effect for an even more striking image. Perfect composition in terms of position of the plane in the image and allowing enough empty space on the right hand side for it to "fly" into</td>', 'A lovely wide angle is a little cliche for planes but works so well. Lovely sky colours and foreground detail. Perhaps a lower camera positon to the ground would have increased the foreground effect for an even more striking image. Perfect composition in terms of position of the plane in the image and allowing enough empty space on the right hand side for it to "fly" into', '2007-11-22 13:57:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4264754, 614059, 67001, '<td valign="top">Beauty</td>', 'Beauty', '2007-11-22 15:23:32.000000', NULL, 1),
