(4271387, 613659, 52549, '<td valign="top">What a lovely image with wonderful colour and clarity. I can''t understand it when people say they can''t look at another drop shot. When it''s as well done as this, it''s a pleasure to look at.</td>', 'What a lovely image with wonderful colour and clarity. I can''t understand it when people say they can''t look at another drop shot. When it''s as well done as this, it''s a pleasure to look at.', '2007-11-27 14:14:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4271446, 614672, 44741, '<td valign="top">I built a similar "potato" gun back in college for a project. It had a 6-inch diameter 10-foot long barrel and fired a 2 lb projectile 1,000 feet up in the air. Lots of fun! I used tennis balls to test it before launching more intricate stuff.<br/> <br/>BTW, great photo!</td>', 'I built a similar "potato" gun back in college for a project. It had a 6-inch diameter 10-foot long barrel and fired a 2 lb projectile 1,000 feet up in the air. Lots of fun! I used tennis balls to test it before launching more intricate stuff. BTW, great photo!', '2007-11-27 14:56:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4271458, 614706, 66253, '<td valign="top">Thanks, everyone. I really appreciate all the specific comments. Clearly lighting is an issue here, and I have no practice lighting indoor subjects. (I usually shoot outdoors, or in bright natural light indoors.) I think my next stop must be the technical tutorials <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=31" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Lighting II: Studio Effects</a> and <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=29" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Intro to Flashes</a> <br/> <br/>I gotta say, after two years of using a point''n''shoot, it was great fun to try my husband''s new camera with real manual controls.</td>', 'Thanks, everyone. I really appreciate all the specific comments. Clearly lighting is an issue here, and I have no practice lighting indoor subjects. (I usually shoot outdoors, or in bright natural light indoors.) I think my next stop must be the technical tutorials Lighting II: Studio Effects and Intro to Flashes  I gotta say, after two years of using a point''n''shoot, it was great fun to try my husband''s new camera with real manual controls.', '2007-11-27 15:05:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4271495, 614695, 66384, '<td valign="top">I like the lighting. Some of the fur, especially along the back of the neck seems over sharpened. And I wish I could see the cats face. But, of course, then it would just be another pet cat photo.</td>', 'I like the lighting. Some of the fur, especially along the back of the neck seems over sharpened. And I wish I could see the cats face. But, of course, then it would just be another pet cat photo.', '2007-11-27 15:27:49.000000', NULL, 0),
