(4271926, 614085, 63269, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bassbone:</b></div><hr/><i> - almost like there are some dust bunnies on your sensor </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>no dust bunnies, dried water drops on background and lens from lots of tries :( </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, I think the ''dust bunnies'' create a neat sort of texture! Sometimes the perfect, spotless photos get a little boring. :)<br/> <br/>I like the colors, and your use of burning on the edges is perfect.</td>', 'Originally posted by eyewave: Originally posted by bassbone: - almost like there are some dust bunnies on your sensor   no dust bunnies, dried water drops on background and lens from lots of tries :(   Actually, I think the ''dust bunnies'' create a neat sort of texture! Sometimes the perfect, spotless photos get a little boring. :) I like the colors, and your use of burning on the edges is perfect.', '2007-11-27 20:34:58.000000', NULL, 0),
